/S /H1
/T (ABSTRACT)
/E (ABSTRACT)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
229 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Forecasting petroleum prices is an essential task due to the significant influence of crude oil on global economic activity, energy markets, transportation, and industrial production. The high volatility and non-linear behaviour of oil prices make accurate prediction challenging, requiring robust statistical techniques to analyse historical patterns and forecast future trends. This project aims to study, analyse, and forecast West Texas Intermediate \(WTI\) crude oil prices using long-term weekly data obtained from the U.S. Energy Information Administration \(EIA\).)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
230 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E <>
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
231 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The ARIMA \(Auto-Regressive Integrated Moving Average\) model was adopted as the primary forecasting technique. Model identification was performed using ACF and PACF plots, and ARIMA\(1,1,1\) was selected based on diagnostic checks and statistical suitability. The model was estimated and validated using SAS procedures, followed by a 26-week ahead forecasting horizon. A Random Walk model was also implemented as a baseline comparator, since it represents the simplest time-series forecasting method.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
232 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Residual diagnostics, including autocorrelation checks and normality tests, validated that the ARIMA model residuals behaved like white noise, indicating a good fit. A comparison between the actual last 26-week average, Random Walk prediction, and ARIMA forecast average demonstrated that the ARIMA model provides a more reliable short-term forecast. Visualisations such as line plots, distribution plots, moving averages, and forecast graphs further supported the evaluation.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
233 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Overall, the project demonstrates the effectiveness of classical time-series techniques for short-term petroleum price forecasting. The study provides insights into market behaviour and establishes a foundation for extending the model with external predictors and advanced machine-learning techniques in future work)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (KEYWORDS:  Time-Series Analysis, ARIMA, Petroleum Price Forecasting, Stationarity, SAS, Random Walk Model)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
