272 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Crude oil, especially West Texas Intermediate \(WTI\), is one of the most widely traded commodities in the world. Volatility in its price can cause major economic impacts, such as inflationary pressure, production cost changes, and fluctuations in financial markets. Traditional economic models often struggle to predict short-term price movements due to the complexity and randomness in market behaviour. Time-series analysis provides a systematic way to study historical price patterns and generate reliable short-term forecasts. This study utilises weekly WTI crude oil data to explore these patterns and build a predictive model.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
