314 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Time-series forecasting of petroleum prices has been widely studied due to the critical role crude oil plays in global economic and industrial systems. Existing research focuses on statistical models, machine-learning approaches, and hybrid techniques to capture the volatile behaviour of oil prices.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
315 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (1. Summary of Past Research)
/E (1. Summary of Past Research)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Classical Statistical Models:)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
317 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E ( Early studies relied on ARIMA models due to their simplicity and strong performance in short-term forecasting. Researchers such as Box & Jenkins demonstrated that ARIMA effectively captures linear dependencies and autocorrelation in time-series data. Several studies found ARIMA suitable for short-horizon crude oil forecasting but limited in handling non-linear patterns and external shocks.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
318 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (GARCH and Volatility Models:)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
319 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E ( Subsequent research introduced GARCH \(Generalized Autoregressive Conditional Heteroskedasticity\) to model volatility clustering in oil prices. These models improved risk estimation but were less effective for long-term value predictions.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
320 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Machine Learning Methods:)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
321 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E ( Recent studies have used Support Vector Regression \(SVR\), Random Forests, and Neural Networks. These methods can capture non-linear relationships but require large datasets and extensive hyperparameter tuning.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
322 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Deep Learning Approaches:)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
323 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E ( LSTM \(Long Short-Term Memory\) networks became popular for crude oil forecasting due to their ability to learn long-term dependencies. Although LSTM outperforms ARIMA in highly volatile periods, it is computationally intensive and harder to interpret.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
324 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Hybrid Models:)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
